{{/*
  The landing page is light on text by rule. Roughly 150 words of prose, no
  paragraph past two sentences, nothing explained here. Every fold is a
  picture, a chart, a command or links, with just enough words to label what
  the reader sees. Explanation lives on the page that owns the topic.

  No em dashes, colons or semicolons in visible text.

  The reader already runs Terraform or OpenTofu. Nothing here teaches state.
*/}}

<section class="hero">
  <h1>choudoufu <img class="hero-icon" src="choudoufu-inline-64.png?v={{.AssetVersion}}" alt="" width="64" height="64"></h1>
  <p class="tagline">IAM-governed state for OpenTofu.</p>

  {{/* The canonical description paragraph (#113): identical wording in
       README.md's opening, this lead, and the GitHub repo description.
       Change all three together or none. */}}
  <p class="hero-lead">Each resource carries its own ownership record as
  ordinary cloud tags. AWS can tell you what an estate contains. Your IAM
  already decides who may read or change it. Experimental, AWS only.</p>

  <p class="hero-sub">A fork of OpenTofu.</p>
</section>

{{/* Fold 1 is the model, because the model is the product.
     Describe it on its own terms. The site used to define itself against a
     state file at every turn, which tells a reader what this is not and
     leaves them to work out what it is. The comparison earns its place once,
     on the model page, for someone who wants the argument. */}}
<section class="pieces">
  <p class="pieces-lead">Three things have to survive between runs.</p>

  <img class="pieces-diagram" src="diagram-pieces.svg"
       alt="Identity as two tags on the resource written by the apply, values in a record store written by choudoufu, effects as a receipt you declare, all three governed by your IAM">

  {{/* The cards do not restate the diagram. Each one adds the consequence
       the picture cannot show, and links to the page that owns it. */}}
  <div class="piece-cards">
    <a class="piece" href="model-identity.html">
      <strong class="piece-home">Identity</strong>
      <span class="piece-note">Pure IAM. Who may change which resource is a
      policy you already know how to write.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="piece" href="model-values.html">
      <strong class="piece-home">Values</strong>
      <span class="piece-note">Resources AWS has no object for.
      <code>null_resource</code>, <code>random_pet</code>,
      <code>time_static</code>.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="piece" href="model-effects.html">
      <strong class="piece-home">Effects</strong>
      <span class="piece-note">A database migration that ran. The plan shows it
      coming before anything fires.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="pieces-more"><a href="model.html">Why they are separate, and what
  it changes</a></p>
</section>

{{/* Fold 2. How far it goes, before any install link. Three charts, three
     denominators, never merged. */}}
<section class="progress">
  <h2>How far it goes</h2>
  {{template "chart" .Lint}}
  {{template "chart" .Crossing}}
  {{template "chart" .IAM}}
</section>

{{/* Fold 3. The command that turns a statistic into a personal answer. */}}
<section class="verdict">
  <h2>Check yours</h2>
  <pre><code>choudoufu live-check</code></pre>
  <p>In your config directory. No credentials.</p>
</section>

{{/* Fold 4. Estates as names and rungs. */}}
<section class="estates">
  <h2>Proven estates</h2>
  <ul class="estate-list">
    {{range .TopEstates 6}}<li>
      <span class="estate-name">{{.Name}}</span>
      <span class="estate-rung {{if .Complete}}estate-complete{{end}}">{{.Reached}}</span>
    </li>{{end}}
  </ul>
  <p><a href="estates.html">All estates</a></p>
</section>

{{/* Fold 5. The destinations. */}}
<section class="docs-nav">
  <h2>Docs</h2>
  <div class="docs-menu">
    {{range .Sections}}<div class="docs-menu-group">
      <h3>{{.Title}}</h3>
      <ul>
        {{range .Items}}<li>{{if .Soon}}<span class="soon">{{.Label}} <em>soon</em></span>{{else}}<a href="{{.Href}}">{{.Label}}</a>{{end}}</li>
        {{end}}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {{end}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="legal">
  <p>Experimental. AWS only. Built on OpenTofu {{.UpstreamVersion}} from fork point
  <a href="https://github.com/opentofu/opentofu/commit/03743ce6e8"><code>03743ce6e8</code></a>.
  Plain OpenTofu is documented at <a href="https://opentofu.org/docs/">opentofu.org</a>.</p>
  <p>MPL-2.0. Not affiliated with or endorsed by OpenTofu or the Linux
  Foundation. OpenTofu is a registered trademark of the Linux Foundation.</p>
</section>

{{/* One chart. Titled bars with their own denominator, because the three on
     this page do not share one. Widths are inline percentages so there is no
     script and it reflows with the page. */}}
{{define "chart"}}
<figure class="chart" id="chart-{{.ID}}">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>{{.Title}}</strong>
    <span class="denominator">{{.Denominator}}</span>
  </figcaption>
  <div class="bars">
    {{range .Bars}}
    <div class="bar-row{{if .Muted}} bar-muted{{end}}">
      <span class="bar-label">{{.Label}}</span>
      {{if .Unmeasured}}
      <span class="bar-unmeasured">{{.Unmeasured}}</span>
      <span class="bar-value"></span>
      {{else}}
      <span class="bar-track"><span class="bar-fill" style="width:{{printf "%.1f" .Percent}}%"></span></span>
      <span class="bar-value">{{.Value}}</span>
      {{end}}
    </div>
    {{end}}
  </div>
  <a class="chart-more" href="{{.Href}}">{{.HrefLabel}}</a>
</figure>
{{end}}
